{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"0e7efe591b024808","name":"card_event_aunt_frieda","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Germany/BloodIron/events/card_event_aunt_frieda","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"AUNT FRIEDA","text":"Give a friendly infantry +1+1. Add TANK MANEUVER to your hand.","flavorText":"The German field manual “Truppenführung” was notable for its clarity. It consisted of a two-part pocket sized manual which was issued to all commissioned officers and senior NCOs. It contained all the basic military doctrine for the German forces and introduced concepts like Command and Battle of the Combined Arms and Mission Command. Rather than a set of rules, it provided guidelines that could be consulted for any situation. It insisted on the importance of delegating operational command and that all subordinates had to understand the commander's intent so they could act on their own initiative. This way of thinking gave the German army an advantage over their enemies while they updated their own tactics and command structure. The manual was affectionately called “Tante Frieda”. A modified form is still used today by the German Army.","faction":"Germany","type":"order","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":1,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_aunt_frieda","title":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_aunt_frieda_title","SourceString":"AUNT FRIEDA","LocalizedString":"AUNT FRIEDA"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Germany","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_aunt_frieda_text","SourceString":"Give a friendly infantry +1+1. Add TANK MANEUVER to your hand.","LocalizedString":"Give a friendly infantry +1+1. Add TANK MANEUVER to your hand."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_aunt_frieda_history","SourceString":"The German field manual “Truppenführung” was notable for its clarity. It consisted of a two-part pocket sized manual which was issued to all commissioned officers and senior NCOs. It contained all the basic military doctrine for the German forces and introduced concepts like Command and Battle of the Combined Arms and Mission Command. Rather than a set of rules, it provided guidelines that could be consulted for any situation. It insisted on the importance of delegating operational command and that all subordinates had to understand the commander's intent so they could act on their own initiative. This way of thinking gave the German army an advantage over their enemies while they updated their own tactics and command structure. The manual was affectionately called “Tante Frieda”. A modified form is still used today by the German Army.","LocalizedString":"The German field manual “Truppenführung” was notable for its clarity. It consisted of a two-part pocket sized manual which was issued to all commissioned officers and senior NCOs. It contained all the basic military doctrine for the German forces and introduced concepts like Command and Battle of the Combined Arms and Mission Command. Rather than a set of rules, it provided guidelines that could be consulted for any situation. It insisted on the importance of delegating operational command and that all subordinates had to understand the commander's intent so they could act on their own initiative. This way of thinking gave the German army an advantage over their enemies while they updated their own tactics and command structure. The manual was affectionately called “Tante Frieda”. A modified form is still used today by the German Army."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BloodAndIron","spawnCardName":"card_event_tank_frieda;card_event_fighter_frieda","soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundCue'AU_Seq_SupplyDrop_1P_Cue'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Misc/Supply_Drop/AU_Seq_SupplyDrop_1P_Cue.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Germany/W